Hi
It sounds like you have reduced the number of unique values of the predictor to the point where the internal working arrays fit within the available memory. End of problem.

> "it was my understanding that secr would not handle multiple levels of a categorical variable well"

'secr' does fine - it's probably just not what you want. Binned numeric data need not be treated as a categorical variable (i.e. a factor). You could still, for example, fit a relationship that was linear on the midpoints of the bins (g0 ~ binnedcc). That requires only one extra coefficient (beta parameter). For factor-valued predictors one extra coefficient is needed for each level (bin?) after the first. You almost certainly don't want that.

Murray

